# Cross-frame DivByZero — the BINDING form (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1c).
# THE CORE-#8 REGRESSION GUARD: the `catch f: match f` form catches MULTIPLE
# categories, so the caller must dispatch on the slot TAG VALUE (not a single
# `slot != 0` branch). A naive single-handler `FaultableCall` routed every fault
# to the FIRST arm → a deep div0 printed 100 (Overflow) instead of 200
# (DivByZero) — a silent miscompile ("both backends agree on 100" is the WRONG
# answer). The per-category tag-dispatch makes the callee's DivByZero tag select
# the DivByZero arm. Expected stdout: 200.
int q(int a, int b): a / b                # may div0; NO local catch

void main():
    int z = 0
    int r = q(10, z) catch f: match f:
        case Fault.Overflow():  100
        case Fault.DivByZero(): 200
    print(f"{r}")
